       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 200 mg for adults. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nThe 1000 mg may be a typo. If so, I can enter one of these:\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg by mouth once daily. Typical starting doses are 50 mg for depression and 25 mg for panic disorder or PTSD.\n- **Maintenance dose:** 50\u2013200 mg by mouth once daily, titrated to response.\n\nTell me the dose and the indication and I'll enter it. If you really do want a dose above 200 mg/day, I can't enter it. That would need to go through pharmacy and the attending."
